# Colours, themes and the /me box

## Editor theme

**Appearance** → **Editor theme** changes the look of the Scene and Status editors. Six themes are included. Restart the script to apply it.

## Colour swatches

The coloured squares in the editors come from **Colour swatches**. Each one has:

| Field | What it does |
|---|---|
| Name | Shown when hovering the square |
| Swatch colour | The square's colour in the editor |
| Game colour code | The code that colours the text in the world, e.g. `~e~` |

The world uses the **game colour code**. The swatch is only a preview. If the preview looks off, adjust **Swatch colour**.

Reorder the list to change the order of the squares.

## Name colours in the /me box

In **/me box name colours by job**, add a job name and a colour. Senders with that job show their name in that colour. Everyone else uses **Default name colour**.

## /me box behaviour

In **/me & overhead text**:

| Setting | Default | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| /me box distance | 6 m | How close someone must be for their /me to reach your box |
| Fade after | 30 s | Auto mode fades the box after this long |
| Visible lines | 7 | Lines before it scrolls |
| Scroll-back size | 50 | Messages kept |
| Delete messages after | 300 s | Each message is removed after this long |

Players control their own box with `/mebox auto`, `persist`, `off`, `move`, `small`, `normal` or `large`.

## Overhead text

**Overhead text time** and **Overhead text distance** control the floating text from `/me`, `/do`, `/id` and `/cash`.

Status tags and scene text use **Scene and status view distance** (General tab) instead.
